# The windows around an action's resolution (zero-vtes docs/rules-digest.md §5.2, §10.1, §10.4;
# rules-qa 5.8, 23.3, 24.1, 24.2, 24.4, 54.1; checked at 1f33be5). A bleed or a political action
# nobody blocks opens a "would be successful" window, the acting Methuselah first, before it
# resolves (Spying Mission, Major Boon, Yawp Court); none once it has failed. Every action that
# resolves, fails or is blocked then has an after-resolution window (Freak Drive). The acting
# Methuselah's next move (resolving, then the next action or the end of the phase) passes each
# window when nobody else would stop it.
# Alice plays first: her prey is Bob, her predator Carol.
seed 25
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *12
library A "Open Motion" *40
crypt B "Marek Hale" *12
library B "Iron Ward" *40
crypt C "Odile Fen" *12
library C "Iron Ward" *40
start

A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
C> move C:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> next
A> next
expect turn 1 A minion

# Carol has a card to play if the bleed would be successful (Major Boon, say): she asks the table
# to wait. So Alice's resolve can't pass the window for her; she passes, Bob passes automatically,
# and Carol plays it (24.2).
A> bleed A:ready:1
B> pass
expect window would-succeed minion
expect waiting A:resolve
C> hold
reject:not-now A> resolve success 2
A> pass
expect impulse C
C> play C:hand:1
# A card played returns the impulse to Alice, and the passes start over; Carol still holds.
expect impulse A
A> pass
expect impulse C
C> pass
expect window none
expect waiting A:resolve
A> resolve success 2 edge
expect pool B 28
log public The action succeeded

# The after-resolution window (5.8), Alice first. Holds end with the window they were asked in,
# so nobody stops this one: Alice's pass closes it.
expect window after-resolution minion
expect impulse A
A> pass
expect action none
expect window none

# A bleed for 0 has no "would be successful": the window just closes, even with Carol holding.
# The action still succeeded, so it has its after-resolution window (24.4).
A> bleed A:ready:2
B> pass
C> hold
A> resolve success 0
expect pool B 28
log public The action succeeded
expect window after-resolution minion
A> pass

# A cancelled action ends at once: there's nothing after it.
A> unlock A:ready:1
A> bleed A:ready:1
A> cancel
expect action none
expect window none

# Bleeding Bob out: he is ousted as the bleed resolves, but the action keeps its after-resolution
# window, without him (24.1).
B> pool -26
expect pool B 2
A> unlock A:ready:1
A> bleed A:ready:1
B> pass
A> resolve success 2
expect ousted B true
expect action bleed A after
expect window after-resolution minion
A> pass
expect action none

# A political action has the would-be-successful window too (54.1); its after-resolution window
# comes after the referendum (5.8). Ending the phase passes it.
A> unlock A:ready:2
A> political A:ready:2 with A:hand:1
C> pass
expect window would-succeed minion
A> resolve success "Alice gains 1 pool"
expect window referendum minion
A> pass
expect window polling minion
A> pass
C> pass
log public The referendum fails (0 for, 0 against)
expect window after-resolution minion
A> next
expect action none
expect turn 1 A influence
